  "Question": "Twenty percent less than \\(60\\) is one-third more than what number?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(16\\)",
    "B": "\\(30\\)",
    "C": "\\(32\\)",
    "D": "\\(36\\)",
    "E": "\\(48\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Twenty percent less than \\(60\\) is\n\\[\n60-\\frac{20}{100}\\cdot60=48.\n\\]\nIncreasing a number by one third makes it \\(1+\\frac13=\\frac43\\) of its original value. Thus \\(48\\) is four thirds of the requested number, which is\n\\[\n48\\div\\frac43=48\\cdot\\frac34=\\boxed{36}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
